# System Design Rule — "Archifyr" Design System

# Archify Project — Always Active

> **Purpose:** This file is the single source of truth for visual implementation — colors, typography, spacing, elevation, shapes, and component styling. Every Tailwind class, every Vue component, and every admin/public screen Cursor generates must conform to this system. It works alongside `project-brief-rule.mdc` (architecture/schema) and `cursor-learning-rule.mdc` (mentorship behavior).

---

## Brand & Style

Built for the high-end architectural and interior design space. The personality is sophisticated, tactile, and quiet — the atmosphere of a premium design studio at night. Modern Minimalism blended with subtle Tactile/Skeuomorphic nuances: deep warm dark tones, material-inspired textures, precise typography. The interface should feel like a physical portfolio — weighted, intentional, expensive. Hierarchy comes from tonal layering and simulated light-source, never from aggressive color or heavy drop shadows.

⚠️ **One deviation from the original Stitch-generated spec, decided for this project:** the original spec calls for a strict, sharp 6px radius everywhere ("avoid pill-shaped, retain rectangular structure"). **We are overriding that** — buttons, inputs, chips, cards, and tables should use a **more rounded, softer radius** across the board (see Section 6 — Shapes for exact values). Everything else in this document stands as specified.

---

## 1. Colors

Rooted in organic, earthy neutrals mimicking charcoal, espresso timber, and terracotta. Never use pure white or pure black.

