## 6. Shapes (⚠️ Updated Radius — Rounder Than Original Spec)

The original Stitch spec called for a strict sharp 6px radius everywhere. **For this build, use a rounder, softer radius scale instead:**

```js
// tailwind.config.js
borderRadius: {
  sm: '0.5rem',     // 8px  — chips, small badges
  DEFAULT: '0.75rem', // 12px — buttons, inputs
  md: '0.75rem',    // 12px — buttons, inputs (alias)
  lg: '1rem',       // 16px — cards, table containers, modals
  xl: '1.25rem',    // 20px — large feature cards, hero panels
  full: '9999px',   // avatars, status dots, circular icon buttons only
}
```

### Applied rules

- **Buttons, inputs, chips/filter pills:** `rounded-md` (12px) — enough to feel soft and modern without becoming a pill
- **Cards (project cards, service cards, stat blocks, admin panel cards):** `rounded-lg` (16px)
- **Tables:** the outer table **container** gets `rounded-lg overflow-hidden` so the header row and last row corners clip cleanly to the radius; individual `<tr>`/`<td>` cells stay square — never round individual table cells
- **Modals/dialogs, drawers, large feature/hero panels:** `rounded-xl` (20px)
- **Avatars, status dots, circular icon-only buttons:** `rounded-full` — this is the one place pill/circular shapes remain correct
- Do **not** apply `rounded-full` to any rectangular button, input, or card — that contradicts the architectural, structured feel of the brand even with the softer radius

💡 **Best Practice:** When building a new component, default to `rounded-lg` for anything card-shaped and `rounded-md` for anything button/input-shaped. If genuinely unsure which bucket a new element falls into, ask rather than guessing — consistency here matters more than getting one component "close enough."

---

## 7. Components

### Buttons

- Primary: `bg-primary text-on-primary rounded-md`, no border
- Secondary: `border border-outline-variant text-on-surface rounded-md bg-transparent`, hover fills subtly with `surface-container-high`
- Disabled: reduce opacity, `text-on-surface-variant`, no hover transition

### Input Fields

- Fill: `bg-surface-container`
- Border: `border-outline`, focus state: `border-primary` with a subtle `ring-primary/20`
- Radius: `rounded-md`
- Labels: `label-lg` style, `text-on-surface`

### Cards

- No box-shadow, ever
- `bg-surface-container border border-outline-variant rounded-lg`
- Hover (if interactive): `hover:bg-surface-container-high hover:border-secondary transition-colors duration-200`

### Tables

- Outer wrapper: `rounded-lg border border-outline-variant overflow-hidden`
- Header row: `bg-surface-container-low`, `label-md` uppercase text, `text-on-surface-variant`
- Rows: `border-b border-outline-variant` between rows, last row no bottom border
- Row hover: `hover:bg-surface-container` (subtle, do not overdo)
- Action icons (edit/delete/view) use `on-surface-variant`, transition to `primary` on hover

### Chips / Filters / Status Badges

- `rounded-sm` (8px), `label-md` text, generous horizontal padding (`px-3 py-1`)
- Active/selected filter: `bg-primary text-on-primary`; inactive: `border border-outline-variant text-on-surface-variant`
- Status badges (Published/Draft, Pending/Contacted): background at ~15% opacity of the semantic color, full-opacity text of that color

### Lists

- Divide items with `border-b border-outline` (not `outline-variant` — slightly more visible for list separation)
- Generous vertical padding per row: `py-6` (24px)

