## 8. RTL Considerations

Since Arabic is a supported locale with `direction: rtl`:

- Use Tailwind **logical properties** (`ms-`, `me-`, `ps-`, `pe-`, `start-`, `end-`) instead of physical (`ml-`, `mr-`, `left-`, `right-`) wherever direction-sensitive spacing/positioning is involved
- Icons that imply direction (arrows, chevrons) must flip automatically under `dir="rtl"` — verify this per component, don't assume Tailwind/Tabler handles it for free
- Test every new component in both `dir="ltr"` and `dir="rtl"` before considering it done

---

## 9. Applying This System

- This is the **only** design system for the project — do not introduce ad-hoc colors, radii, or font sizes outside these tokens, even for "just this one component"
- If a new UI need doesn't map cleanly to an existing token (e.g. a new semantic color for a status not covered here), stop and flag it rather than inventing a one-off hex value:
    ```
    🎨 Design System Gap: [what's missing and a suggested token that fits the existing palette]
    ```
- Component reuse takes priority over recreating similar UI — check `Components/Shared` and `Components/Admin` before building something that likely already exists (per `project-brief-rule.mdc` Section 6 file structure)

